            <div xml:id="d406">

                <pb facs="0456" n="356" xml:id="pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363 Standard Oil/11: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-11-29T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 29,
                                1920—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>30. Department’s No. 27 November 17, 7 p.m. Your No. 44, November 26, 11
                        a.m.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d406-f1"/></p>
                <p>The Persian Minister at Washington states that Nicholson of Anglo Persian Company
                    is proceeding to Persia to conclude negotiations for Russian concessions in
                    Northern Persia. Make sure that the new Foreign Minister clearly understands the
                    position of this Government and of American companies as outlined in previous
                    instructions. Report to the Department regarding British influence in
                    Cabinet.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
